<!-- Welcome Section -->

## Welcome

This professional learning module is designed to help you prepare to teach Unit 1: Logic-Based AI from CodeAI's **AI Foundations Year 2** curriculum, available at <a href="[INSERT AIF Y2 COURSE LINK]" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">AI Foundations Year 2</a>.

AI Foundations Year 2 is a year-long course for high school students, built as part of a Career and Technical Education (CTE) pathway aligned to the Microsoft Azure AI-901 certification exam.

<!-- Goals Section -->
<div style="margin: 20px auto; width: 90%; max-width: 900px; background: #FFFFFF; border: 1px solid #E4E2F8; padding: 20px; border-radius: 10px; box-shadow: 2px 2px 8px rgba(0,0,0,0.1); font-size: 14pt;">
    <h2>In this module, you will:</h2>
    <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
        <li>Explain AI as a spectrum of approaches, from simple rule-based logic to today's generative systems, so students see it as many tools, not one black box.</li><br>
        <li>Read and reason through foundational Python: variables, functions, and loops, well enough to support students writing it for the first time.</li><br>
        <li>Connect hands-on activities like hill climbing, decision trees, and debugging exercises to the reasoning skills they build, not just the code that results.</li><br>
        <li>Recognize where rule-based, logic-driven AI breaks down, and why that limitation sets up the shift to machine learning in Unit 2.</li><br>
        <li>Understand how AI Foundations Year 2 aligns to the Microsoft Azure AI-901 certification, so you know which concepts carry exam weight and which don't.</li>
    </ul>
</div>

**Suggested Total Time:** [CONFIRM: full Unit 1 module time]

**Lesson One Suggested Time:** 10 minutes

